<title>GERMANY: Bonn news conference on coal talks 0900 GMT.</title>
<headline>Bonn news conference on coal talks 0900 GMT.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1997-03-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>The German government said on Thursday it would hold a news conference at 10 a.m. (0900 GMT) on the outcome of crisis talks on coal subsidies between Chancellor Helmut Kohl and miners' union leader Hans Berger.</p>
<p>The talks began at 9 a.m. (0800 GMT) amid reports that the government was prepared to offer some more money to cushion the immediate blow of sharp subsidy cuts which the government plans between now and 2005. Chancellery Minister Friedrich Bohl and Economics Minister Guenter Rexrodt were due to attend the news conference.</p>
</text>
